| [[Tianwu of Zong|Emperor Tianwu]] || 1209 || 1231–1273 || None || 1273 || [[House of Yuanlong]] || Reform ruler who mandated the central adoption of the [[Societal Assembly]] and presided over the transition into imperial court government; also initiated Zong's programme of marriage diplomacy with the [[Jyunhap]] and [[Three Luoyan States]]
|-
| [[Tianhe of Zong|Emperor Tianhe]] || 1246 || 1273–1302 || None || 1302 || [[House of Yuanlong]] || Consolidated the court state; oversaw the peak of maritime commerce with the [[Sanese archipelago]]; his marriage to [[Fenglan of Bingzhou|Princess Fenglan]] in 1271 established the personal union with [[Bingzhou]] that would later trigger the [[Jade Sea War]]
|}

The imperial title developed out of the later unification period, when the final rulers of the [[House of Yuanlong]] transformed the kingdom into the [[Jade Empire]]. The early imperial order retained the same dynastic house, but the succession now passed through a more formal court process in which elite assent and assembly confirmation mattered alongside hereditary legitimacy.

